# Runtime diagnostic messages
hbmcompat.debug.reason.tank_fill_failed=cannot fill input tank %s with [%s]: tank holds %s. Drain leftover fluid of another type, or the batch exceeds tank capacity.
hbmcompat.debug.reason.item_slot_rejected=cannot place %s into input slot %s: the slot holds an incompatible item, or the amount exceeds the stack limit (machine limit %s, item limit %s)
hbmcompat.debug.reason.fluid_slots_short=recipe needs %s input fluids but this machine has only %s input tanks
hbmcompat.debug.reason.fluid_mismatch=input fluids do not match the recipe: recipe wants [%s], AE2 supplied [%s]. Pressurised recipe fluids are never accepted, and the ME fluid must be the Forge mirror this mod registers for that HBM fluid.
hbmcompat.debug.reason.item_slots_short=recipe needs %s distinct item inputs but this machine has only %s input slots
hbmcompat.debug.reason.item_mismatch=input items do not match the recipe: recipe wants [%s], AE2 supplied [%s]. Turn off substitution on the pattern (AE2 may hand over an ore-dict stand-in the HBM recipe rejects) and check the pattern amounts equal the recipe exactly.
hbmcompat.debug.reason.tank_incompatible=input tank %s holds %s of %s, which this recipe cannot use (it wants [%s], matched tank-by-tank in order). Drain that tank.
hbmcompat.debug.reason.tank_not_empty=recipe needs no input fluid but an input tank still holds some. Drain the input tank(s).
hbmcompat.debug.reason.auto_switch_ambiguous=recipe %s is ambiguous with %s in auto-switch group '%s': both accept the first input, so the machine would switch away by itself. This recipe cannot be automated through the adapter.
hbmcompat.debug.reason.blueprint_missing=recipe %s is blueprint-pooled and the blueprint in the machine's blueprint slot (slot 1) does not cover it. Insert the right blueprint.
hbmcompat.debug.reason.acidizer_identifier=acidizer fluid identifier conflicts with the recipe; change or remove it
hbmcompat.debug.reason.acidizer_recipe=supplied item selects a different acidizer recipe; check pattern substitution
hbmcompat.debug.reason.unreadable_inputs=AE2 handed over inputs this adapter cannot read (an unsupported stack type, or a non-ME crafting table). Nothing to push.
hbmcompat.debug.reason.no_machine=no machine adjacent to this adapter: the targeted side holds no supported HBM machine, or its multiblock core could not be resolved (try breaking and replacing the machine)
hbmcompat.debug.reason.machine_busy=machine on the %s side is busy: it is mid-cycle, or its input slots still hold un-consumed items
hbmcompat.debug.reason.recipe_unmatched=no unique HBM recipe matches this pattern on the %s. Inputs must match exactly; pressurised fluids are unsupported. Mixer patterns must also declare the exact fluid output and amount. For assembly and chemical recipes with identical inputs, outputs must select one candidate.
hbmcompat.debug.reason.pattern_changed=this pattern is stamped for %s/%s but now matches %s/%s. Re-encode the pattern.
hbmcompat.debug.reason.pending_items=the adapter still has items waiting to be sent back into the network
hbmcompat.debug.reason.adapter_inactive=the adapter is not active: no channel or no power. Note that the side the adapter points at cannot carry the ME cable — run the cable to another face.
hbmcompat.debug.reason.pattern_unregistered=this pattern is not registered on this adapter (its pattern slots do not hold it)
hbmcompat.debug.reason.crafting_locked=crafting is locked on this adapter: %s
hbmcompat.debug.reason.import_attempt=ticking: source ok, attempting import
hbmcompat.debug.reason.source_unsupported=gate: target can never be a fluid source (not an HBM machine/storage core, core unresolved, or machine w/o output tank e.g. arc welder/soldering station)
hbmcompat.debug.reason.chunk_unloaded=gate: target chunk not loaded
hbmcompat.debug.reason.bus_inactive=gate: proxy inactive (no channel/power?)
hbmcompat.debug.reason.source_unavailable=no fluid source tank available right now (storage tank not in send/both mode, or all output tanks empty/pressurized); polling
hbmcompat.debug.reason.grid_error=idle: grid access exception
hbmcompat.debug.reason.no_work=no move: nothing to do
hbmcompat.debug.reason.export_unconfigured=no fluid configured in bus GUI (nothing to export)
hbmcompat.debug.reason.export_success=OK: exporting fluid into machine input tank
hbmcompat.debug.reason.sink_unavailable=no fluid sink tank at target (not an HBM machine/storage core, core unresolved, or storage tank not in receive/both mode)
hbmcompat.debug.reason.bus_idle=idle: proxy inactive or target chunk unloaded
hbmcompat.debug.reason.fluid_unmapped=configured fluid '%s' is not an HBM fluid (no mapping)
hbmcompat.debug.reason.tank_unconfigured=no input tank already set to %s (tank full, untyped, typed for another fluid, or pressurized); the bus never changes a tank's fluid type, so set it via the machine's recipe or the tank's own GUI first
hbmcompat.debug.reason.tank_full=input tank for %s is full
hbmcompat.debug.reason.network_empty=ME network has no %s to extract (or no power)
hbmcompat.debug.reason.mixer_recipe_busy=mixer still has pending inputs or is processing another recipe; wait before switching
hbmcompat.debug.reason.mixer_identifier=mixer fluid identifier selects a different output; remove or change it
hbmcompat.debug.reason.mixer_output_blocked=mixer output tank contains another fluid, is pressurised, or lacks room for one result
hbmcompat.debug.reason.mixer_input_tank=mixer input tank %s contains fluid incompatible with the selected recipe
